                        "entry_id": "722479ae-45f4-3f4e-a49b-1aebc66fc0b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een kind dat liegt (jokt)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "kindertaal"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3fabfffa-86f9-3228-b401-54d68d953975",
                        "entry_id": "722479ae-45f4-3f4e-a49b-1aebc66fc0b5",
                        "glosses": [
                            "een volwassen persoon die op een kinderachtige en doorzichtige manier liegt"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "b637c296-4302-4c78-8260-c4fc6c9989a2",
                                "sense_id": "3fabfffa-86f9-3228-b401-54d68d953975",
                                "text": "Toch werd de gaswinning in 2013 niet verlaagd, maar verhoogd, naar 53,9 miljard kuub. In dat jaar waren er 133 aardbevingen. Ter vergelijking: in 2008 werd er 41,2 miljard kuub gewonnen. In 2007 28,9. Dus als minister-president Rutte zegt dat de gaswinning ‘bijna gehalveerd’ is, dan weten de Groningers heus dat de 27,6 miljard kuub in 2016 niet echt de helft is van wat er vroeger gewonnen werd. Dus als je dan zegt ‘netjes’, dan zit je een beetje te jokkebrokken."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "ee0cdc71-d25b-492e-b868-e631571e8352",
                                "sense_id": "3fabfffa-86f9-3228-b401-54d68d953975",
                                "text": "In het Mauritshuis, hoor ik, kwam het enige kritische geluid van Henk Krol, de onverstoorbare jokkebrok van 50Plus. „Als je ziet hoeveel mensen boven de 45 jaar zonder werk zitten en hoeveel ouderen worden gekort”, zei hij, „zou ik het geld toch echt anders willen besteden.” Met zulke vijanden heeft Rembrandt geen vrienden meer nodig."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "f899e5dd-611f-4595-99f2-4e50c0172bc2",
                        "source_entry_id": "722479ae-45f4-3f4e-a49b-1aebc66fc0b5",
                        "source_sense_id": "4093a294-9e64-30bc-b086-09798a3625f8",
                        "source_sense_description": "(kindertaal) een kind dat liegt (jokt)",
                        "target_lang_word": "liar",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "liar",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48ddd1cf-0bb5-3559-baeb-049aefa083b7",
                                        "entry_id": "0beb25d9-8f5a-3d24-8e96-c043c68a5b3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A person who frequently lies; someone who tells a lie."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26315097-df91-4787-b96e-b10142725470",
                                                "sense_id": "48ddd1cf-0bb5-3559-baeb-049aefa083b7",
                                                "text": "She paused and took a defiant breath. ‘If you don't believe me, I can't help it. But I'm not a liar.’ ¶ ‘No,’ said Luke, grinning at her. ‘You're not dull enough![…]What about the kid's clothes? I don't suppose they were anything to write home about, but didn't you keep anything?[…]’"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "a4877bce-a2bd-3c4d-b23f-2d125d063da4",
                                        "entry_id": "0beb25d9-8f5a-3d24-8e96-c043c68a5b3f",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A swabber responsible for cleaning the outside parts of the ship rather than the cabins, a role traditionally assigned to a person caught telling a lie the previous week."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "74b14fb9-d5f1-4632-8d73-329ae21dfc9a",
                                                "sense_id": "a4877bce-a2bd-3c4d-b23f-2d125d063da4",
                                                "text": "The Swabber is to keep the Cabbins, and all the Rooms of the Ship clean within board, and the Liar to do the like without board. The Liar holds his Place but for a week; and he that is first taken with a Lie upon a Monday morning, […] for that week he is under the Swabber, and meddles not with making clean the Ship within board, but without."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b14ac5f7-2b53-4beb-9e5e-b685328fa22c",
                                                "sense_id": "a4877bce-a2bd-3c4d-b23f-2d125d063da4",
                                                "text": "The swabber, perhaps the lowliest position on the ship, was responsible for cleaning the decks. By tradition, each Monday a new crewmember was appointed the liar—the first person caught telling a lie the previous week."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    }
